{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And the stranger.</b> When the stranger accepts not to worship idolatry, do not oppress him in your land because you have far greater power than him. And remember that you were strangers like him. And just as He mentioned the stranger who has no power, so too the orphan and the widow, who are Israelites and have no power. And after He said לא תענון (you shall not oppress them) in plural language, He said אם תענה (if you oppress), for anyone who sees a person oppressing an orphan and a widow and does not help them is also considered an oppressor."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:37:24.971944479Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}